Enhancement: `vaultic repair snapshots --forget` removes broken snapshots

In the past vaultic had no command to remove broken snapshot files.

`vaultic repair snapshots --forget` can now remove broken snapshot files,
which have been found previously by `vaultic check` or by earlier error messages from vaultic commands.

For example, `vaultic repair snapshots --forget 1d204771` will remove a broken snapshot file with id `1d204771`.

https://github.com/vaultic/vaultic/issues/21892
